    "note": "Evidence of the torn process list that stopped campaign events-v3-20261108. The probes read a copy of session 46 restored from its archive (values.restore), moved to data/diagnostics/torn-walk-20261112/events-v3-20261108_46_test_events_write_heavy/raw next to copies of the session's metadata files, because the parser takes the guest boot identity from session.json beside raw/; the session directory and the archive of the campaign are unchanged. page_read_order relies on the collector reading guest physical memory in ascending order in chunk_bytes pieces (vmicollect/src/backend.c, vmic_capture_timed). nodes hold the task_struct fields as read from each snapshot image. The forward walk has two torn spots. At the middle node its prev still names a node that the same image shows deleted from the list (prev LIST_POISON2, next the middle node): the worker process and its database backend left the list during the read, after the middle node's page and before the pages of the nodes around them. A stale prev alone does not stop the forward walk. At the tail node the page holds a live thread of the orders process (exit_state 0, PF_EXITING clear, mm set), while init_task.prev and the previous node's next, read later, already name it: during the read that thread exited, its task_struct was reused and a new task was linked at the tail into it (snapshot 271 shows kworker/1:2 in it). Alone, that tail insertion is the shape the rule tail of b065ee4 closes. Together, the first torn link is the middle node, which init_task.prev does not name, so the rule tail does not apply; and the backward walk starts on the stale tail page and jumps from it to the leader's predecessor, so it does not pass the forward nodes before the first torn link and the rule prev of 0b61ffd does not apply either. The row was refused. forward_before_tail_node shows that the forward nodes up to the tail node differ from both neighbours only by the processes that ended or started around the event; it is a consistency check, not an accepted list. The owner decided not to change guestparse (extractor_sha256 of the bundle and of corpus benign-v6), so this shape stays a known limitation."
